# SQL's `SELECT a FROM t` written as `| project a from t`: the table comes first (DS0153), no fix.
mode: syntax
---- query
from x | project a from t
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..26
  PIPELINE@0..18
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "x"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    PROJECT_OP@9..18
      IDENT@9..16 "project"
      WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@17..18
        NAME_REF@17..18
          IDENT@17..18 "a"
  WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
  PIPELINE@19..25
    IDENT@19..23 "from"
    WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
    NAME_REF@24..25
      IDENT@24..25 "t"
  WHITESPACE@25..26 "\n"

error[DS0153]: in DataScript the table comes first
  --> query:1:20
  |
1 | from x | project a from t
  |          --------- ^^^^ SQL's `FROM` after the column list
  |          |
  |          the columns are chosen here
  |
  = help: start the query with the table, then pipe it into the operator: `from t | project a`
